  abstract: (
    content: [
随着多模态大语言模型在图像理解、视觉问答、智能助手等场景中的广泛应用，其安全性问题已由传统文本空间扩展到图文联合空间。现有多模态越狱研究表明，攻击者可通过图像文字嵌入、视觉扰动和图文联动提示等削弱模型的安全对齐能力，但已有方法仍存在风险语义暴露明显、图像模态主要承担静态载荷，以及在现实黑盒部署下迁移性与稳定性不足等问题。

论文面向多模态大语言模型安全评估，提出一种基于图像语义嵌入的跨模态联合越狱攻击方法。该方法将目标风险语义拆分为图像侧可承载、可识别的语义线索，并在文本侧设计恶意语义对齐、编码引导、多轮推理与注意力转移机制、结构化输出模板诱导四个组件。通过图像语义嵌入与文本恢复链的配合，方法能够在跨模态推理过程中逐步恢复隐藏语义，从而削弱多模态系统的安全防护。

论文在 SafeBench 五个敏感任务类别的 250 条样本上开展实验。结果显示，完整方法在 gpt-4o、grok-3 和 qwen-vl-max 上分别取得 87.60%、95.60% 和 93.20% 的平均攻击成功率（ASR），平均查询次数（QN）分别为 1.96、1.37 和 1.65，显著优于 FigStep 基线（ASR / QN 分别为 33.20%/3.85、47.20%/3.21、42.00%/3.49）。gpt-4o 上的消融实验表明，去除编码引导、图像侧 PGD 语义嵌入、多轮推理与注意力转移机制、结构化输出模板诱导或恶意语义对齐，都会造成 11.60 至 16.80 个百分点的 ASR 下降，说明各组件均对整体效果有明显贡献。实验结果表明，图像语义线索与文本恢复链的组合能够提高攻击输入的可解析性与触发效率，同时也暴露出当前多模态系统在处理跨模态隐藏语义和多步恢复任务时的安全风险。论文工作可为多模态大语言模型安全评估提供参考。
    ],
    keywords: ("多模态大语言模型", "越狱攻击", "图像语义嵌入", "跨模态联动", "安全评估"),
  ),
  abstract-en: (
    content: [
With the wide application of multimodal large language models in image understanding, visual question answering, intelligent assistants, and other scenarios, safety concerns have gradually extended from the pure-text domain to vision-language interactions. Existing studies on multimodal jailbreak attacks have shown that attackers can weaken safety alignment through typographic image embedding, visual perturbations, and image-text linkage prompts. However, existing methods still suffer from obvious risk semantic exposure, the image modality mainly serving as a static payload, and insufficient transferability and stability under real black-box deployment.

This thesis investigates multimodal large language models and proposes a cross-modal linkage jailbreak attack method based on image semantic embedding. The proposed method refines the target risk semantics into image-side loadable and identifiable semantic clues and introduces malicious semantic alignment, encoded guidance, multi-round reasoning and attention shift mechanism, as well as structured output template induction in the text modality. By combining image semantic embedding with multi-round textual reasoning, the method forms a cross-modal hidden semantic recovery chain that effectively bypasses the safety defenses of multimodal systems.

Experiments conducted on 250 samples from five sensitive task categories in SafeBench demonstrate that the method achieves average attack success rates of 87.60%, 95.60%, and 93.20% on gpt-4o, grok-3, and qwen-vl-max, with average query numbers of 1.96, 1.37, and 1.65, respectively, substantially outperforming the FigStep baseline (ASR/QN of 33.20%/3.85, 47.20%/3.21, and 42.00%/3.49). Ablation experiments on gpt-4o reveal that removing the encoding guidance, image-side PGD semantic embedding, the multi-round reasoning and attention shift mechanism, the structured output template induction, or the malicious semantic alignment leads to ASR reductions ranging from 11.60% to 16.80%, highlighting the contribution of each component. These findings suggest that combining image semantic cues with textual reconstruction can improve both the interpretability and triggering efficiency of attack inputs, while also exposing notable weaknesses of current multimodal systems in handling hidden cross-modal semantics and multi-step reconstruction tasks. The results may provide useful insights for future safety evaluation of multimodal large language models.
    ],
